 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "58:1-4 is not glossed: the tafsirs divide «بفضل الله وبرحمته» differently (Al-Muyassar: Islam and the guidance; As-Sa'di: the Quran, then the religion). A book for «موعظة», light for «وهدى ورحمة», coins for «مما يجمعون», wheat for «من رزق». STAGING v4: c1 (57-58): a town by day. Mankind addressed (57:1-2) is a mixed group of five faceless people (men and women) on the right; the believers (three men in light robes) sit on the left and read (57:6, 57:13: the Quran, an admonition, a healing and a guidance for the believers, both tafsirs); a book plate for the admonition (57:5-6, gone before 57:7), a light plate for guidance and mercy (57:12 to 58:1, never starting on the Name), the camera on the believers for 57:14. 58 is the Prophet's ﷺ instruction (say): nobody gestures in it, no plate starts on 58:1; the camera on the believers for in that let them rejoice (58:5) and on the people for what they amass (58:10), with a coins plate for the worldly goods (58:9-10, As-Sa'di: the goods of this world). c2 (59): the Prophet's ﷺ rebuke to the polytheists who forbade some of Allah's provision: farmland by day with a camel (both tafsirs name animals, Al-Muyassar also plants) and the polytheists (three faceless men in dark robes). They make no gesture inside his words (camera only): the camera on the camel and a wheat plate for provision (59:7-10), on them for you made some unlawful (59:9), and for do you invent about Allah (59:17); a geometric plate for has Allah permitted you (59:15-20). No particular animal ruling is drawn."
 },
